  },
  "note": "Macromodel of Milliken, Silva-Martinez and Sanchez-Sinencio, IEEE TCAS-I 54(9) 2007, Fig. 8, with the Tables II/III values at Iout = 0: CGS = 100 pF, CGD = 26 pF, Cout = 100 pF, Rf1 = 156 k, Rf2 = 124 k, Cf2 = 1 pF, Cf = 20 pF, Rf = 200 k. GP = 286 uS and Rds = 30 k are this benchmark's reading at the 10 uA divider current; GE Re = 20, G1 R1 = 20, Gf1 = 286 uS (the weak-inversion limit at 10 uA), Gf2 R2 = 31.6 (30 dB, Table III), the parasitics Ce, C1, C2 are this benchmark's choice within the paper's stated gains. Loop opened at Vfb: V1 drives GE, vfb is the return."
 },
